  "patch": {
    "approval": "coordinator REPLY-16 item 1 (option A)",
    "purpose": "A library must not end the process. Every path that ended the process with exit status 1 returns an error to the caller, and the diagnostics that were written to stderr are removed; the engine adapter maps each return to the decision 0040 status and stage.",
    "files": [
      "src/gemm.cuh",
      "src/kernels.cu",
      "src/kernels.h",
      "src/mma884.cuh",
      "src/repack.cu",
      "src/repack.h"
    ],
    "changes": [
      "gemm.cuh gemm::launch returns cudaError_t: cudaErrorInvalidValue for a bad shape, the cudaFuncSetAttribute error for the shared-memory opt-in, else cudaGetLastError() after the launch.",
      "mma884.cuh prepare_x returns nullptr when its allocation or memset fails (freeing a partial allocation); launch_packed and launch return cudaError_t (memset error, cudaErrorMemoryAllocation, or cudaGetLastError()).",
      "repack.cu: the [[noreturn]] unsupported() helper is removed; ggml_row_bytes and tiled_vecs return 0 for an unknown type, to_q8_0 returns no converter, and repack returns bool (false for an untiled type or bad shape).",
      "kernels.cu: check_launch is removed; gemm_launch, matmul and pack_f32 return cudaError_t, and matmul returns cudaErrorInvalidValue for an unsupported type.",
      "Includes made unused by the removals (<cstdio>, <cstdlib>, <cfloat>) are dropped."
    ],
    "gate": "No call of the process-ending functions exit or abort, and no fprintf to stderr, in engine/vendor/xavier-qwen/ or engine/src/kernels/cuda/.",
    "alignment_fix": {
      "purpose": "write_xf read a 4-byte aligned __half2[4] local array as a uint4, a misaligned 16-byte local read (undefined behaviour). compute-sanitizer on sm_86 reported 'Invalid __local__ read of size 16 bytes ... misaligned' and the launch failed with 'misaligned address (status 716)'.",
      "files": [
        "src/kernels.cu"
      ],
      "change": "kernels.cu adds pack_half2x4, which copies the four __half2 values into 32-bit words and builds the uint4 with make_uint4 (the pattern mma884.cuh pack_x uses); both write_xf branches (rowmajor and fragment order) call it. The stored values and the xf layout are unchanged.",
      "found_by": "compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck, sm_86 (RTX 3090)"
    }
  },
